dment was to change the wording of South Australian Senator [Penny Wong](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/sa/penny_wong)'s (Labor) original motion. ### Amendment text > *Omit paragraphs (c) to (e), substitute:* > >> *(c) notes the actions of the President in addressing the matter as soon as the Senate sat following the speech, recognising that when the Governor-General is in the chair the President cannot exercise the usual powers or authority to manage the chamber as the President would on a typical sitting day;* >> >> *(d) calls on:* >> >>> *(i) all senators to respect our democratic institutions, including our Parliament, to engage in debates and commentary respectfully, and to refrain from inflammatory and divisive actions that reflect poorly on the Senate, both inside and outside the chamber, and to uphold the standards of the Senate at all times, and* >>> >>> *(ii) Senator Faruqi to apologise for the unparliamentary conduct, disrespect of proceedings and disregard for the position of the Governor-General as our Head of State and conventions of our parliamentary democracy;* >> >> *(e) in the event Senator Faruqi fails to apologise for the unparliamentary conduct, calls on the President to report to the Senate that Senator Faruqi has committed an offence in accordance with standing order 203 so that a motion may be moved that Senator Faruqi be suspended from the sitting of the Senate; and* >> >> *(f) in light of this conduct, does not regard it as appropriate for Senator Faruqi to represent the Senate as a member of any delegation during the life of this parliament.* ### Original motion text > *That the Senate—* > >> *(a) expresses its profound disapproval of Senator Faruqi's disrespectful protest and actions contrary to standing orders during t","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-9633","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2025-07-23/1"}
